== the facts as they were built, in the order they are stored
check ascription Impl : B@B
check interface Impl : A@A
check ascription Impl : A@A
check ascription Impl : A@A
dep B@B -include-> A@A
dep A@A -alias-> <B>
dep B@B -include-> A@A
equal B = A
equal A = A
equal A = B
omission: affected=none source=B reason=unresolved-module
omission: affected=A@A source=none reason=unsupported-path
omission: affected=none source=B reason=unresolved-module
== normalized: sorted, deduplicated, equalities oriented
check ascription Impl : A@A
check interface Impl : A@A
check ascription Impl : B@B
dep A@A -alias-> <B>
dep B@B -include-> A@A
equal A = B
omission: affected=none source=B reason=unresolved-module
omission: affected=A@A source=none reason=unsupported-path
== normalizing is idempotent
normalize (normalize t) = normalize t: true
ensure_normalized t = normalize t: true
compare normalizes what it is given: true
== merging two overlapping sets
check ascription Impl : A@A
check argument Impl : C@C
dep B@B -include-> A@A
dep C@C -alias-> B@B
equal A = B
equal A = C
omission: affected=none source=B reason=unresolved-module
omission: affected=C@C source=none reason=unresolved-module-type
== merging is commutative and merge_many folds it
merge left right = merge right left: true
merge t t = t: true
merging with empty changes nothing: true
merge_many [] = empty: true
merge_many [a; b; c] = merge (merge a b) c: true
distinct sets compare unequal: true
